mt6885: VDEC, VDEC2 and MDP power domains off when idle (reverts 0052)

The decoder powers its subsystem down when idle now (cezanne-vdec runtime
PM; a power cycle no longer darkens the block since 0050's MDPSYS SMI
gate fix), so genpd may turn VDEC / VDEC2 / MDP off. They were the last
blockers of the SPM's dram / syspll / bus26m constraints.

(Regenerated 2026-11-02 against the tree the earlier patches produce: an unexported
intermediate change had set VDEC / VDEC2 to ALWAYS_ON; this now goes straight from 0046's
KEEP_DEFAULT_OFF to no caps.)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6885-pm-domains.h b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6885-pm-domains.h
index 140309287..b668f1dfa 100644
